# =====================================================================
# CRITICAL: the ~20 GB of unrelated dirs that made every EAS upload fail
# (archive limit is 2 GB → "Compressing project files" hung/failed → 0 builds).
# Verified by `du -sh */`. These are NOT part of the RN app — and the list is
# SURGICAL: it excludes ONLY unrelated subprojects, NOT anything the build needs
# (patches/, plugins/, assets/, src/, *.config.js are intentionally kept).
# =====================================================================
all function action/
AiMarketingtool-pro-fbaf2fa/
Xcode_27_beta/
macports-ports/
my-app/
my-project/
cargo/
foodie/
nuxt-nightly/
marketingtool/
marketing-tool/
# Leading slash = repo-ROOT only. Without it, `tools/` also matched
# src/screens/tools/ and stripped the app's tool screens from the build.
/tools/
/starter-workflows/
/mac-cli/
/learn-terraform-init/
/learn-terraform-modules-use/
/my_gem/

# Security: secrets must never reach the EAS build archive.
# If a future build needs an EXPO_PUBLIC_* value from .env, mirror it in
# EAS environment variables (eas env) instead of shipping the file.
.env
.env.*
*.keychain
